---
import { BASE } from './model';
// Commands as in README.md (quick start) and docs/BENCHMARKING.md (the smoke recipe's four steps).
---
<section class="rule" id="start">
  <div class="wrap qs">
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow">Quick start</p>
      <h2>Serve the systems, then run the benchmark</h2>
      <p class="lede">Requires Python 3.11 or later. The servers alone cost nothing to run; benchmark runs call real models.</p>
      <ol>
        <li><b>Install</b> the package and its dev tools.</li>
        <li><b>Serve</b> every system, or point any MCP client at one.</li>
        <li><b>Run</b> the 6-task smoke recipe end to end, then open its report.</li>
      </ol>
      <p class="note">Runs use the Claude Code harness, the one built so far. Another agent, an SDK or a model's API can be <a href={`${BASE}/get-started/add-a-harness/`}>added as a harness</a>; pull requests are welcome.</p>
    </div>
    <div>
      <div class="code">
        <div class="code-h"><span>Serve the systems</span><span>shell</span></div>
        <pre><code><span class="p">$ </span>pip install -e ".[dev]"
<span class="p">$ </span>python -m mockmcp serve
<span class="c"># every system at http://127.0.0.1:8800/&lt;system&gt;/mcp</span></code></pre>
      </div>
      <div class="code">
        <div class="code-h"><span>Run the smoke recipe</span><span>shell</span></div>
        <pre><code><span class="p">$ </span>python -m mockmcp eval recipe bench/recipes/smoke.yaml \
    --out runs/smoke --harness claude-code
<span class="p">$ </span>python -m mockmcp eval run runs/smoke --model haiku --workers 4
<span class="p">$ </span>python -m mockmcp eval grade runs/smoke \
    --judge claude-code --judge-model sonnet
<span class="p">$ </span>python -m mockmcp eval report runs/smoke --html</code></pre>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
